W: 2. Father, dear father, you've done me great wrong,
W: You have married me to a boy is too young,
W: I'm twice twelve and he is but fourteen,
W: He's young but he's daily growing.
W:
W: 3. Daughter, dear daughter, I've done you no wrong,
W: I have married you to a great lord's son,
W: He'll make a lord for you to wait upon,
W: He's young but he's daily growing.
W:
W: 4. Father, dear father, if you see fit,
W: We'll send him to college for one year yet,
W: I II tie blue ribbons all around his head,
W: To let the maidens know that he's married.
W:
W: 5. One day I was lookin' o'er my father's castle wall,
W: I spied all the boys a-playin' with the ball,
W: My own true love vas the flower of them all,
W: He's young but he's daily growing.
W:
W: 6. At the age of fourteen, he was a married man,
W: At the age of fifteen, the father of a son,
W: At the age of sixteen, his grave it was green,
W: And death had put an end to his growing.
